## Change the rule while the desk keeps working

The old [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is an accepted,
immutable record from 11 June 2024. Its subject-only rule is superseded by
[decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause).
The live [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) now follows the replacement rule.

Read the report body. Establish product, tenant, date order, entry channel,
form version, expected result, and actual result. Merge only when the evidence
supports the same cause as an open ticket. Same subject is not enough;
different subjects can describe the same cause. Unknown tenant, unmatched
product, or conflicting symptom evidence means **keep separate and investigate**.
The explorer shows the exported routing model, not proof of a production fix.

Page freshness is also evidence: the old triage and decision were last reviewed
in 2024. Read their stale warnings and check the rendered components, not just
the prose. A recent review date on the old incident did not make its one-bug
claim true.

## Verify before closing

- Keep one report ID in one cause ticket; preserve report membership and intake-tag disagreements.
- Test day-first parsing with ambiguous and unambiguous dates, and retain month-first behavior.
- Test booking-v3 hint/parse agreement for each affected tenant locale, including a browser/tenant locale mismatch.
- Reproduce the flagged timing symptoms before deciding whether they need another ticket.
- Check received reports after each actual deployment. This export cannot prove that either fix shipped.

